! Shower of Born-only LO events as in the CMS production configuration of gg -> ZH at LO (public CMSSW
! Configuration/Generator Pythia8PowhegEmissionVetoSettings_cfi): the CMS POWHEG emission-veto block
! on LO events whose SCALUP = sqrt(s-hat) = m_ZH, i.e. a power
! shower (pTmaxMatch 2) in which every ISR/FSR emission with POWHEG pT above m_ZH is vetoed.
! nFinal = -1 (Pythia's default since 8.309): no strict count of the final state.  With the strict count
! (CMS: 2) PowhegHooks counts the final-state particles at the end of the record, which for our ggxy
! LO events are the H -> b bbar daughters appended by the process-level Higgs decay; nFinal = 3 aborts
! the run.  The veto is the same either way: pThard = 0 sets the veto scale to SCALUP for
! every event, and no POWHEG emission is identified (the b quarks have the Higgs as mother).
POWHEG:nFinal = -1
POWHEG:veto = 1
POWHEG:vetoCount = 100
POWHEG:pThard = 0
POWHEG:pTemt = 0
POWHEG:emitted = 0
POWHEG:pTdef = 1
SpaceShower:pTmaxMatch = 2
TimeShower:pTmaxMatch = 2
